.TH FUZZYGENE 1 2000-1月 "fuzzygene_model_config" "fuzzygene_model_config"
.SH NAME
fuzzygene_model_config \- The configuration attached to a model (identical to \fBconfig.json\fR inside the package).
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIfuzzygene_model_config(\fBfuzzygene\fR as <generic> FuzzyGeneModel, 
[\fB<Environment>\fR]);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The configuration attached to a model (identical to \fBconfig.json\fR inside the package).
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBfuzzygene\fB \fR\- a trained (or restored) model. 
.PP
.PP
\fBenv\fB \fR\- the R# runtime environment used to report errors. 
.PP
.SH VALUE
.PP
the configuration object
.PP
.SH DETAILS
.PP
Useful to confirm what the model was actually fitted with, especially the rule budget
 (\fBmaxRules\fR / \fBmaxConsequentParams\fR) and \fBnoveltyQuota\fR. Remember that
 \fBmaxRegulators\fR / \fBmfCount\fR are only upper bounds: the real structure is reduced by the
 rule budget, which is reported on the \fBstructure:\fR line of \fBfuzzygene_report\fR.
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
FuzzyGene
.SH FILES
.PP
biosystem.dll
.PP
